XR window: what its mask cuts in front of its plane is not drawn (the pop-out volume as a clip)

WakerQuest 1.1.5. The window's eyes are masked (patch 0030): in front of its plane only the rectangle
narrowing toward the game camera's eye (the pop-out volume) shows. What the head's frustum draws there
outside that volume (branches near the camera, beside the window) took the EFB's pixels and the mask cut
them to alpha 0: the room showed through, in their shape, instead of the game behind them. Patch 0031's
clip plane already keeps the pop-out's front; this adds its sides.

- GX_AURORA_SET_POPOUT_CLIP / AuroraSetPopoutClip(tableFromView, depth): the window's table from the view
  delta's target space (as the mask's, x and y within +-1, z in metres toward the player) and the game
  camera's depth. Off at the end of each frame.
- The GX uniform header gets xr_win (four vec4f: the table's rows, then the depth and 1 when on), written
  as zeros when off or for draws the view delta does not apply to; MaxUniformSize grows by 64.
- The fragment shader discards what is in front of the window's plane and outside the narrowing
  rectangle, as the mask's test (stereo.cpp, its window branch).

